      "why": "iterative is included as a baseline to map the area-accuracy trade-off at low throughput. It will almost certainly fail the throughput constraint (throughput = Fmax/(N+3), so at 100 MHz with N=14, that's only ~5.9 Msps), but it provides the smallest-area reference point on the Pareto front for accuracy. This helps establish the lower bound of the trade-off curve and ensures the hypervolume calculation has a well-defined reference. The budget is small because it's unlikely to be on the feasible front, but it's useful for context."
