  "rationale": "The spec has a hard throughput constraint of >= 32 Msps, which is very demanding. In my assigned families (iterative and unrolled_k), only unrolled_k can plausibly meet this, and only with high k (4-8) and high Fmax. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) requires data_width and n_iter to be sufficient; from CORDIC theory, N=12-16 iterations with W=14-16 should give ~12-14 bits of accuracy, so I'm narrowing the ranges to focus the search. The system constraint (p99 batch latency <= 0.5 us) is also critical: 32 requests must complete within 0.5 us. For unrolled_k with k=8 and 5 cycles per result, 32 results take 160 cycles. At 160 MHz, that's 1 us, which exceeds 0.5 us. So we need even higher Fmax or higher k. This is a tight problem. I'm allocating 70% of the budget to unrolled_k to explore the feasible region, and 30% to iterative as a baseline. The data_width range is 14-16 because W=14 gives output LSB of 2^-12, which just meets the error constraint with minimal iterations, while W=16 gives more margin. n_iter is 12-16 to balance accuracy and area. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small (0-2) to minimize area while maintaining accuracy."
